    {
      "ordinal": 6,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "3.2",
      "title": "Transitional Style Helmets",
      "body": "In the middle of the 14th century, Bascinets with a side-pivoting visor began to be depicted in miniatures and art. They include a longer visor with no chin plate and will represent the majority of helmets until the middle of the 15th century.\n\nTransitional style helmets are Approved for 14th century and Transitional armors.\nTransitional style helmets are Denied for 15th century armors.",
      "page_from": 5,
      "page_to": 5,
