    {
      "ordinal": 12,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "4.2",
      "title": "Visor",
      "body": "The visor must not be too long or too short, it must conform to the proportions of historical sources.\nThe pivots must be reproduced as per historical sources.\nIt is permitted to weld the visor down. A welded visor must resemble a functional removable visor.\n\nIt is permitted to add metal plates to protect the throat. Such a plate must be strong enough to endure full-contact fighting and must be concealed under the aventail.\n\nA leather strap can be used to secure the visor.\n\nBreath holes should be round and must not exceed a diameter of 10 mm. Breath holes must not be so numerous that they compromise the helm’s structural integrity. It is acceptable to mirror breath holes to both sides.\n\nBreath holes of other shapes must be documented by historical sources to be permitted.",
      "page_from": 8,
      "page_to": 8,
      "stable_key": "side-pivoting-visored-bascinets:4.2",
      "parent_key": "side-pivoting-visored-bascinets:4",
      "review_status": "extracted",
