    {
      "ordinal": 13,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "4.3",
      "title": "Eye slots",
      "body": "Eye slots should resemble sources for the visor.\nEye slots should not exceed 25 mm tall to prevent any injury.\n\nSide-pivoting visored Bascinets with historical evidence of externally riveted Eye bars can add up to two (2) externally riveted eye bars per eye slot.\n\nHelmets that are currently documented with externally riveted Eye bars are Sugarloaf and Romance of Alexander.\n\nSide-pivoting visored Bascinets with two (2) Eye slots are permitted to add up to two (2) safety Eye bars per Eye slot.\n\nSide-pivoting visored Bascinets with a single Eye slot are permitted to add up to five (5) safety Eye bars: one (1) in the middle and two (2) on each side.\n\nExample:\n\nPicture from Medieval Extreme ©\n\nSide-pivoting visored Bascinets with historical evidence of integrated Eye bars can use some, such as the following:\n\nBL Royal 20 C VII Chroniques de France ou de St Denis - 1380/1400 - France\n\nEye bars must conform to the “Eye bars” document.",
      "page_from": 8,
